  "body": "## Problem\nA setup with a part alignment is refused on lathe, plasma, wire and sinker machines.\n\n## Done means\n- Decide for each machine type what a part alignment means.\n- A proof test for each machine type that accepts it.\n\nParent: #2276. The maintainer said on 2026-11-16: \"why would i not be able to reorientate my part?! or rotate my WCS's..\"\n\nThe rule of #2276: remove a refusal only with its proof test. The proof test cuts the kind in a turned setup and in the same part with the turn baked into its mesh. The two documents must post the same program. The part as modelled must cut a different path or refuse. See `crates/app/tests/setup_align_2d_kinds.rs` and `setup_align_hole_kinds.rs`.\n\nSafety: a kind that reads the model frame in a turned setup cuts in the wrong place. Keep the refusal until the proof test passes.\n",
